# Skill: Subsumption Architecture

> A Grok skill for a priority stack: Provide air, Eat, Win, Talk. Higher layers stop lower ones.

## Purpose
Explain the four-layer stack so anyone can see life support beats mission, and mission beats talk. Source: fitzyracing1/skill-subsumption-architecture.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Provide air first.
2. Eat second.
3. Win the mission third.
4. Talk last, and only if the upper layers are quiet.

## Key ideas
- Subsumption (a higher need can stop a lower one)
- Provide air (keep the environment livable)
- Eat (get energy)
- Win (do the assigned job)
- Talk (report and listen)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/skill-subsumption-architecture
provide_air()   # first
eat()           # second
win()           # third
talk()          # last
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. provide_air() → “keep air and environment first”
2. eat() → “get energy next”
3. win() → “do the job after that”
4. talk() → “speak only when the rest is handled”

## Decisions the program makes
- If air is missing → stop eat, win, and talk
- If energy is missing → stop win and talk
- If the mission is active → stop talk

## What a person would notice
The robot will not chat while it cannot breathe.

